<http://purl.org/nanopub/temp/np1/assertion> {
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-lmc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/Claim> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-lmc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label> "Local mate competition sex ratio" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-lmc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/description> "When a few mothers lay eggs on a patch and their offspring mate there before the daughters disperse, the evolutionarily stable sex ratio is female-biased, and the bias weakens as the number of mothers grows." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-lmc> <http://www.w3.org/1999/02/22-rdf-syntax-ns#type> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/TestableHypothesis> .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-lmc> <http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#notation> "unbeatable proportion of males x^* = \\frac{n-1}{2n} for n foundresses per patch (diploid case)" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-lmc> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/context> "Assumptions: n foundresses per patch, mating confined to the natal patch, only females disperse, mothers control the sex ratio. Formal status: proved as an ESS within the model. Haplodiploidy and inbreeding shift x* slightly." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-lmc> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/proposedTest> "Vary the number of foundresses per host in a parasitoid wasp (e.g. Nasonia) and compare the offspring sex ratio with (n-1)/(2n)." .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-lmc> <https://w3id.org/delphi/ontology/hypothesisType> "model-theorem" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-lmc> <http://purl.org/dc/terms/source> "W. D. Hamilton (1967) Extraordinary Sex Ratios" .
  <https://w3id.org/delphi/resource/claim/hamilton-lmc> <http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#seeAlso> <https://doi.org/10.1126/science.208.4448.1157> .
}
